 "reco_text": "Consider redesigning the weed management program with a stronger pre-emergence residual targeting pigweeds, barnyard grass, and broadleaf species to close the gap that allowed early-season escapes.\n\nBe ready to spray a fungicide targeting Gray Leaf Spot, Northern Corn Leaf Blight, and Rust at the VT window if in-field and regional foliar disease pressure are similar to this season. Crop rotation and debris management reduce the risk of Gray Leaf Spot and Northern Corn Leaf Blight next year by minimizing overwintering fungus.\n\nReview nutrient timing, placement, and loss mitigation practices. Consider soil sampling the affected areas and adjusting the fertility program before planting to address persistent potassium deficiency.\n\nConsider a targeted response to stink bug at the R1\u2013R3 window next season if pressure develops \u2014 monitor for stink bug presence beginning at early reproductive stages.\n",
 "reco_id": "1312437",
